replace('docs/releases/release-1.8.2.md', '## Conversational retrieval', '## Developer references\n\nThe new [MCP developer guide](../mcp-developer-guide.md) explains all 28 public tools: why they exist, request examples, response limits and implementation/test ownership. The separate [CLI developer guide](../cli-developer-guide.md) covers every public command and guarded management workflow. Both are linked from the root README and documentation index, link to each other, and explain the 18-tool native terminal catalog versus the 28-tool unified MCP catalog, including offline CLI drafts versus live reviewed UI proposals.\n\nLinux CI exposed a fixture race acquiring the writer lock after native worker readiness: short maintenance turns can still own that lock. The concurrent MCP reader regression now waits within 30 seconds only for typed OS lock contention, then holds the actual lock throughout both reads. Other errors remain failures. This shared test correction applies to Windows and both Apple CPU builds as well; it changes no product admission, integrity checks or query assertions. Platform validation is recorded separately from this correction.\n\n## Conversational retrieval')
